## Playwright tests with every change

Every new or changed feature ships with matching Playwright coverage in `playwright/`; see the "Playwright tests with every change" section of `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`.

- Add or update the specs under `playwright/tests/api` and `playwright/tests/ui` in the same change, and run the affected specs before declaring it complete.
- Do not delete, disable, or weaken existing tests to make a change pass.
- This is a student capstone: implement only required behavior and avoid unnecessary complexity.

# Design documentation (record of decisions)

Major or important design decisions **must** be documented on file under `design/`. That folder is the source of truth for team alignment — do not leave the design only in chat, only in a README, or only in code comments.

## What counts as major

Document (or update) a design doc when the change affects any of:

- Auth / identity (login, passwords, JWT)
- Tenancy and multi-dealer boundaries
- Roles and permissions
- API contracts (REST shapes, error model, versioning)
- Gateway routing and BFF behavior
- Classroom acceptance / demo flows

Other cross-cutting product or architecture choices that the team must not diverge on also belong in `design/`.

## Source of truth vs summaries

- **Canonical**: Markdown under `design/` (English only; repo-relative paths — same as `english-docs`).
- **OK to summarize or link**: root `README`, `design/PREP-CHECKLIST.md`, `env.example`, and similar entry points — they must point at the `design/` doc, not replace it.

## Same-change rule

When implementing or changing such a design, update the relevant `design/` document **in the same change**. Prefer editing an existing doc over inventing a parallel one; add a new file only when the topic is new.

```text
<!-- BAD -->
Ship auth/tenancy behavior; leave the decision in chat or only in README

<!-- GOOD -->
Update design/<topic>.md and implement; README may link to that file
```
